## Summary

I have opensycl-0.9.4 installed that provides ```include/CL/sycl.hpp```

Configure attempts to compile this code to find SYCL:
```
#include <CL/sycl.hpp>

int main(){
   sycl::queue q(sycl::default_selector{});
   return 0;
}
```

This fails because opensycl defines the ```hipsycl::sycl``` namespace instead of ```sycl```.

Compilation of this code succeeds:
```
#include <CL/sycl.hpp>

int main(){
   hipsycl::sycl::queue q(hipsycl::sycl::default_selector{});
   return 0;
}
```

What package provides the ```cycl``` namespace? Can ```opensycl``` be used?


