I received an email from a research associate who works with the TACC
Stampede cluster, who noted problems with file appending. Please see the
following information and proposed fix.

We recently found some output files are corrupted if the users running
with -append option to restart the simulation, which is default since
version 4.5. The simulation is running normally without any issues and
the trajectories are corrupted. I have identified the problem. When the
simulation is continued with appending, the output files will be
truncated first.

However, ftello tends to give the incorrect file position on parallel
file system on Stampede (Lustre 2.1), which leads to the problematic
truncation and data corruption. I am also able to reproduce the problem
with a toy code as long as fopen mode is “a” or “a+”. It is more likely
a bug in Lustre 2.1 and we have contacted with the Lustre team.
Meanwhile, the problem could be fixed by seeking the file position to
the end of the file, as shown in red below in the source code
src/gmxlib/gmxfio.c. I have tested a few example with the patch and it
seems working fine. If it is confirmed as a Lustre bug, the same problem
could exist on more than Stampede. I am wondering if the Gromacs team
could patch the fix in the future distribution.

Proposed patch:


    static int gmx_fio_int_get_file_position(t_fileio *fio, gmx_off_t *offset)
    {
        char buf[STRLEN];

        /* Flush the file, so we are sure it is written */
        if (gmx_fio_int_flush(fio))
        {
            char buf[STRLEN];
            sprintf(
                buf,
                "Cannot write file '%s'; maybe you are out of disk space or quota?",
                fio->fn);
            gmx_file(buf);
        }

        /* We cannot count on XDR being able to write 64-bit integers, 
         so separate into high/low 32-bit values.
         In case the filesystem has 128-bit offsets we only care 
         about the first 64 bits - we'll have to fix
         this when exabyte-size output files are common...
         */

    // added by TACC
        gmx_fseek(fio->fp, 0, SEEK_END)
    //
        *offset=gmx_ftell(fio->fp);

        return 0;
    }


