It appears that the names of energy components related to Nose-Hoover
temperature coupling are stored in the .edr file incorrectly (or
conversely, accessed incorrectly). The problem is that in mdebin.c
(starting at line 303 in the latest release-4-5-patches):

      if (etc == etcNOSEHOOVER) {
        for(i=0; (i<md->nTC); i++) {
          ni=groups->grps[egcTC].nm_ind[i];
          sprintf(buf,"Xi-%s",*(groups->grpname[ni]));
          grpnms[i]=strdup(buf);
        }
    ...
      }

However, if an .edr file is read using get\_enx\_state(), as in grompp
when an .edr file is used instead of a .cpt file, the names include the
NH chain length value (line 1117 in enxio.c):

    for(j=0; (j<state->nhchainlength); j++)
        {
              sprintf(buf,"Xi-%d-%s",j,bufi);
              state->nosehoover_xi[i] = find_energy(buf,nre,enm,fr);
              sprintf(buf,"vXi-%d-%s",j,bufi);
              state->nosehoover_vxi[i] = find_energy(buf,nre,enm,fr);
        }

It seems to me that mdebin.c should be modified to read:

      if (etc == etcNOSEHOOVER) {
        for(i=0; (i<md->nTC); i++) {
          ni=groups->grps[egcTC].nm_ind[i];
          for (j=0; j<state->nhchainlength; j++)
          {
              sprintf(buf,"Xi-%d-%s",*(groups->grpname[ni]));
          }
              grpnms[i]=strdup(buf);
        }
    ...
      }

I don’t know if this affects anything else, so I’m not changing it
myself unless someone who knows .edr I/O better can verify that this fix
is appropriate.


