implements the intention of the equations in manual section 4.3.3.

I say the **intention** of 4.3.3, because I think equation 4.75 should
read “phi’ = (phi-phi\_0) MOD (-PI,+PI\]” or such, equation 4.76 should
not mention phi\_0, and it should be expressed more clearly in the text
that \\delta phi is the deviation at which the restraint potential
should begin to act. Also, there is no dihedral\_restraints entry in
table 5.6. I’m happy to fix those if we agree that’s how they should
read.

The relevant code is:

/\* phi can jump if phi0 is close to Pi/-Pi, which will cause huge  
\* force changes if we just apply a normal harmonic.  
\* Instead, we first calculate phi-phi0 and take it modulo (-Pi,Pi).  
\* This means we will never have the periodicity problem, unless  
\* the dihedral is Pi away from phiO, which is very unlikely due to  
\* the potential.  
\*/  
